# =============================================================================
# RUNTIME DATA — never commit (Phase 17 / SEC-17-06)
# =============================================================================
# The SQLite database and the uploads directory were NOT ignored. Committing
# them would have published, in plain view of anyone with repository access:
#   - every account's email address and scrypt password hash
#   - every squad's PRIVATE join code and squad password hash
#   - every live session token (a valid token is an account takeover)
#   - every participant's submitted evidence files
#
# These are runtime artefacts, not source. The schema lives in
# prisma/schema.prisma and prisma/migrations/; the database is rebuilt with
# `npm run db:migrate && npm run db:seed`. Upload directories are created on
# demand by the application.
#
# If this repository has ALREADY been pushed with a database committed, adding
# these rules is not sufficient — the data remains in git history. Rotate every
# credential and purge the history before treating it as clean.

# SQLite database and its WAL/shared-memory sidecars
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/prisma/*.db
/prisma/*.db-journal
/prisma/*.db-wal
/prisma/*.db-shm

# Participant submissions and Creator-managed level resources
/uploads/

# Database backups
/backups/

# Level 3 bug catalogue. Holds no flags (ORION owns those), but the point values
# are competition configuration, so real event files stay out of the repository.
prisma/level3-catalogue.json
prisma/level3-catalogue.*.json
!prisma/level3-catalogue.example.json

# Test datasource — points at a disposable database the suites truncate.
.env.test
